      "id": "2re720f",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Constitutional Articles Related to State Government"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Articles 153 to 167 in Part VI of the Indian Constitution deal with the State Executive.",
        "The Governor is the constitutional/nominal head of the state executive, while the Chief Minister is the real executive authority.",
        "The Council of Ministers is collectively responsible to the Legislative Assembly (Vidhan Sabha) of the state.",
        "Only six states in India currently have a bicameral legislature containing both Vidhan Sabha and Vidhan Parishad.",
        "The Legislative Assembly is a directly elected house with a normal term of 5 years, while the Legislative Council is a permanent body."
      ],
      "id": "j8d3rpo"
    },
