    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Article 213 empowers the Governor to promulgate ordinances when the state legislature is not in session.",
        "The 6 states with bicameral legislatures are Andhra Pradesh, Telangana, Uttar Pradesh, Bihar, Maharashtra, and Karnataka.",
        "The minimum age required to be appointed as Governor is 35 years.",
        "The Legislative Council (Vidhan Parishad) cannot be dissolved; 1/3rd of its members retire every second year."
      ],
